    </section>

    <section class="local-seo-band" aria-label="Local service area">
      <p>
        Located in Greenwood Village near the Denver Tech Center, Eden serves peptide
        therapy patients from Denver, Cherry Hills Village, Centennial, Englewood,
        Littleton, and the south Denver metro.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="quick-answer-section" aria-labelledby="quick-answer-heading">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Quick answer</p>
        <h2 id="quick-answer-heading">What is Wolverine Stack peptide therapy at Eden?</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="quick-answer-card">
        <p>
          The Wolverine Stack at Eden Health Clubs is a clinician-guided BPC-157 + TB-500
          peptide protocol in Greenwood Village for adults who want structured recovery,
          mobility, and active-aging support with medical director oversight.
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Location:</strong> Greenwood Village, serving Denver, DTC, Cherry Hills, Centennial, Englewood, and Littleton.</li>
          <li><strong>Best fit:</strong> Active adults who want a recovery conversation before ordering peptides online.</li>
          <li><strong>Care model:</strong> Eden medical wellness club consult, licensed provider review, pharmacy fulfillment when prescribed.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="copy-section copy-section--lead">
      <p class="eyebrow">BPC-157 + TB-500</p>
      <h2>The recovery stack people ask for when rest is not enough.</h2>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          You can stretch, ice, modify workouts, take a week off, and still feel like your
          body is negotiating with you every morning. That is usually the moment people
          start looking for the Wolverine Stack.
        </p>
        <p>
          The stack pairs BPC-157 and TB-500 into a clinician-guided protocol designed to
          support tissue repair pathways, soft-tissue mobility, and recovery capacity. It
          earned the Wolverine name because it is one of the most recognized peptide
          combinations in the recovery world.
        </p>
        <p>
          At Eden Health Club in Greenwood Village, the Wolverine Stack is not handed out
          casually. Your protocol starts with a consultation, medical review, and a clear
          recommendation so you know whether this is actually the right starting point.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="copy-section copy-section--split">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Local peptide therapy</p>
        <h2>Close to Denver. Built for the south metro lifestyle.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="prose prose--tight">
        <p>
          Eden Health Club is located at 5990 S University Blvd in Greenwood Village,
          minutes from the Denver Tech Center and a short drive from Cherry Hills,
          Centennial, Englewood, and Littleton.
        </p>
        <p>
          This matters because peptide therapy should not feel like a faceless shipment.
          Denver-area patients can start with a local consult, ask real questions, and
          receive guidance from a care team that understands active Colorado lifestyles.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="copy-section copy-section--split">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Who it is for</p>
        <h2>For Denver adults who are too young to feel this limited.</h2>
      </div>
      <ul class="check-list">
        <li>You are 40–50 and your recovery suddenly feels older than your lifestyle.</li>
        <li>You train, ski, hike, lift, run, golf, or play court sports and feel it for days.</li>
        <li>Your joints, tendons, or soft tissue keep making you scale back.</li>
        <li>You are post-procedure or post-injury and want a structured recovery conversation.</li>
        <li>You have heard about peptides but want medical guidance, not internet guesswork.</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="note-box">
        The cost of waiting is not just discomfort. It is fewer workouts, more hesitation,
        and slowly saying no to things you still want to do. Eligibility is determined
        during consultation.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="ingredient-grid">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <p class="eyebrow">What is in it</p>
        <h2>Two peptides. One focused recovery conversation.</h2>
      </div>
      <article>
        <h3>BPC-157</h3>
        <p>
          BPC-157 is studied for its role in supporting localized tissue repair, tendon and
          ligament recovery, and gut lining support. In the Wolverine Stack, it is commonly
          discussed as the more targeted repair-support peptide.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <h3>TB-500</h3>
        <p>
          TB-500 is studied for its role in systemic recovery, mobility, soft-tissue
          remodeling, and circulation support. In this stack, it is commonly discussed as
          the broader recovery-support peptide.
        </p>
      </article>
      <p class="note-box note-box--wide">
        Why pair them? The combination is popular because it addresses recovery from more
        than one angle. Eden reviews your goals, history, and risk factors before
        determining whether the stack makes sense for you.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="process-section" id="how-it-works">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <p class="eyebrow">How it works at Eden</p>
        <h2>A premium protocol should not feel like a mystery shipment.</h2>
      </div>
      <ol class="step-list">
        <li>
          <div>
            <strong>Consultation.</strong>
            Review what is actually slowing you down: soreness, mobility, training load,
            injury history, medications, and goals.
          </div>
        </li>
        <li>
          <div>
            <strong>Protocol design.</strong>
            If you are a candidate, Eden explains the recommended subcutaneous injection
            protocol, what to expect, and how follow-up works.
          </div>
        </li>
        <li>
          <div>
            <strong>Pharmacy fulfillment.</strong>
            Your protocol is fulfilled through a U.S. licensed compounding pharmacy when
            prescribed.
          </div>
        </li>
        <li>
          <div>
            <strong>Delivery & onboarding.</strong>
            First-time users can receive injection guidance so the process feels clear,
            private, and manageable.
          </div>
        </li>
        <li>
          <div>
            <strong>Follow-up.</strong>
            Your care team checks in so you are not left guessing whether to continue,
            adjust, or explore a different protocol.
          </div>
        </li>
      </ol>
    </section>

    <section class="copy-section copy-section--split">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Why Eden</p>
        <h2>Local, polished, and built for people who expect discretion.</h2>
      </div>
      <ul class="check-list">
        <li>Located in Greenwood Village for Denver, DTC, Cherry Hills, and Centennial patients.</li>
        <li>A high-touch medical wellness club environment, not a research-peptide checkout page.</li>
        <li>Clinician-guided care with medical director oversight before treatment.</li>
        <li>U.S. licensed compounding pharmacy fulfillment when prescribed by a licensed medical provider.</li>
        <li>Consultation, onboarding, and follow-up under one local care team, with easy connection to functional medicine, peptide injections, wellness injections, and fitness + performance.</li>
      </ul>
      <div class="internal-link-grid" aria-label="Related Eden services">
        <a href="https://edenhealthclubs.com/functional-medicine/">Functional Medicine</a>
        <a href="https://edenhealthclubs.com/functional-medicine/peptide-injections/">Peptide Injections</a>
        <a href="https://edenhealthclubs.com/functional-medicine/wellness-injections/">Wellness Injections</a>
        <a href="https://edenhealthclubs.com/fitness-performance/">Fitness + Performance</a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="pricing-section">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Pricing</p>
        <h2>Know the right protocol before you pay for the wrong one.</h2>
        <p>
          Pricing is reviewed during your consultation because your recommendation depends
          on your goals, eligibility, and protocol design. If Wolverine is not the best
          fit, Eden will tell you that before you commit.
        </p>
      </div>
      <a class="button button--primary" href="#consult">Check availability</a>
    </section>

    <section class="testimonial-section">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <p class="eyebrow">Demand signals</p>
        <h2>The people asking about this stack are not trying to slow down.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="testimonial-grid">
        <blockquote>They want to keep skiing, lifting, hiking, golfing, and traveling without planning life around soreness.</blockquote>
        <blockquote>They are tired of being told to “just rest” when rest has not restored the way they move.</blockquote>
        <blockquote>They want a private, clinician-guided option before another month of scaling everything back.</blockquote>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="faq-section">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <p class="eyebrow">FAQ</p>
        <h2>Common questions before you book.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-list">
        <details>
          <summary>Is the Wolverine Stack FDA-approved?</summary>
          <p>
            BPC-157 and TB-500 are not FDA-approved drugs. They are compounded by a
            licensed U.S. pharmacy when prescribed by a licensed medical provider.
          </p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>Is it legal?</summary>
          <p>
            Yes, when prescribed by a licensed medical provider and compounded by a licensed
            pharmacy. Eden does not sell research-only peptides over the counter.
          </p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>How is it administered?</summary>
          <p>
            The Wolverine Stack is administered by subcutaneous injection. First-time users
            get an in-club walkthrough so the first dose is not a guessing game.
          </p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>How long until I notice anything?</summary>
          <p>
            Most people report changes in recovery, soreness, or mobility within 2–4
            weeks. Tissue-level repair typically takes longer, often 6–8 weeks.
          </p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>Can I stack this with GLP-1, TRT, or other peptides?</summary>
          <p>
            Often, yes, but only after Eden's clinical team reviews your full protocol. We do that
            during consultation.
          </p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>Where is Eden?</summary>
          <p>
            Eden Health Club is located at 5990 S University Blvd in Greenwood Village,
            Colorado, near the Denver Tech Center. Eden serves Denver, Cherry Hills
            Village, Centennial, Englewood, Littleton, and the broader south Denver metro.
          </p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>Do you see patients from Denver or only Greenwood Village?</summary>
          <p>
            Eden sees patients from across the Denver metro. Many peptide therapy consults
            come from Denver, DTC, Cherry Hills, Centennial, Englewood, and Littleton
            because the club is easy to access from the south metro.
          </p>
        </details>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="split-section" id="consult">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Start here</p>
        <h2>Do not let another month become your new normal.</h2>
        <p>
          If your body is starting to dictate what you can do, start with a consult. Eden
          will review your goals, explain your options, and tell you honestly whether the
          Wolverine Stack is the right fit.
        </p>
        <p class="microcopy">
          New peptide consult availability is limited each week. Greenwood Village health club
          or telehealth available.
        </p>
      </div>
      <LeadForm cta="Request My Peptide Consultation" />
    </section>

    <section class="legal-section">
      <p>
        Statements on this page have not been evaluated by the Food and Drug
        Administration. BPC-157 and TB-500 are not FDA-approved drugs and are dispensed
        only when prescribed by a licensed medical provider and fulfilled by a licensed compounding pharmacy under applicable
        state and federal regulations. Information on this page is educational and is not a
        substitute for personalized medical advice. Eligibility is determined during
        clinical consultation.
      </p>
    </section>

    <nav class="eden-action-bar" aria-label="Contact Eden">
      <a href="tel:+17206057678">
        <span>Phone</span>
        <strong>Call Now</strong>
      </a>
      <a href="mailto:care@edenhealthclubs.com">
        <span>Email</span>
        <strong>Care Team</strong>
      </a>
      <a href="#consult">
        <span>Consult</span>
        <strong>Book</strong>
      </a>
    </nav>
  </main>
